      "text": "To solve the expression \\(1 + 6 \\cdot 2 - 3 + 5 \\cdot 4 \\div 2\\), we must follow the order of operations, often remembered by the acronym PEMDAS (Parentheses, Exponents, Multiplication and Division (from left to right), and Addition and Subtraction (from left to right)).\n\nStep 1: Perform the multiplications and divisions from left to right.\nFirst, we do \\(6 \\cdot 2 = 12\\).\nNext, we do \\(5 \\cdot 4 = 20\\), and then divide 20 by 2, which gives \\(20 \\div 2 = 10\\).\n\nThe expression now simplifies to \\(1 + 12 - 3 + 10\\).\n\nStep 2: Perform the addition and subtraction from left to right.\nFirst, do \\(1 + 12 = 13\\).\nNext, do \\(13 - 3 = 10\\).\nThen, do \\(10 + 10 = 20\\).\n\nAs we get to the end of the expression without needing further operations, our final answer is \\(\\boxed{20}\\).",
