      "text": "First, we need to evaluate exponents or roots. However, in this case, there aren't any.\nNext, we solve operations with parentheses, also called grouping symbols, so there are no parentheses in our problem.\nNext, addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division are performed from left to right. We can work our way through it like this:\n$1+6\\cdot2-3+5\\cdot4\\div2 = 1+6-3+5\\cdot4\\div2$\nWe follow our order of operations here, so we multiply and divide as we move left to right. We also group addition and subtraction on the left to right:\n$1+6-3+5\\cdot4\\div2 = 1+6-3+20\\div2$\nNow we divide as we go left to right:\n$1+6-3+20\\div2 = 1+6-3+10$\nLast we actually add left to right:\n$1+6-3+10 = 7-3+10$ \n$7-3+10 = 4+10$ \n$4+10 = \\boxed{14}$ \nI hope this video helped you on your way to learning how math problems are worked out. If there is something you want to discuss, please leave a comment below. Have a great day! The final answer is $\\boxed{14}$.",
